feat(pornmd): add cross-site search provider

Corrects an earlier conclusion in this project. A previous investigation
looked only at /c/asian, saw no video cards, and concluded PornMD was
client-rendered and therefore unusable. That was wrong: the search and
popular pages do server-render results, and search is the site's whole
purpose.

What was actually there all along:
- Cards are div.card[data-public-id] with the title on <a title>, the cover
  on an img served from c*.ttcache.com, and duration/quality in .badge.
- Each card links to /out/?l=<base64>, which decodes to
  <garbage><source url><NUL><base64 JSON metadata>>. The real target is
  recovered by pulling printable ASCII out of the decoded bytes.
  230 of 240 links decode (96%); the rest are dead on the source side.

Playback comes from the source sites, not from PornMD, so support is split
per source. Measured distribution over 230 decoded results:
  www.eporner.com  154 (67%)
  xh.partners       34 (15%)
  xgroovy.com        6
  18 others        1-2 each
Implemented eporner and xh.partners (82% combined) and made the rest fail
with an explicit "source site not supported" rather than guessing a URL.

Verified: list 109, search "Asian" 115, meta 5/5, stream 6/6 on implemented
sources. /new and /rating return 403, so they are not offered as entries.
